1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,656
This card makes you spend up to twice as much.

2
00:00:02,726 --> 00:00:04,551
And your brain doesn't even notice.

3
00:00:04,921 --> 00:00:09,173
At MIT, researchers auctioned tickets to a sold-out basketball game.

4
00:00:09,443 --> 00:00:11,582
Half the bidders could only pay in cash.

5
00:00:11,702 --> 00:00:13,168
The other half? Credit card.

6
00:00:13,488 --> 00:00:15,626
The card group bid up to double.

7
00:00:15,746 --> 00:00:18,617
Same seats. Same game. Twice the price.

8
00:00:19,037 --> 00:00:21,942
Psychologists call it, the pain of paying.

9
00:00:22,112 --> 00:00:25,818
When you hand over cash, brain regions linked to pain light up.

10
00:00:25,888 --> 00:00:27,075
You feel the loss.

11
00:00:27,445 --> 00:00:29,491
But a tap? A swipe? No pain.

12
00:00:29,611 --> 00:00:32,307
The money leaves, and the feeling never arrives.

13
00:00:32,727 --> 00:00:34,761
That's why casinos use chips.

14
00:00:34,831 --> 00:00:36,274
Why apps save your card.

15
00:00:36,344 --> 00:00:38,773
Why buy now, pay later exists.

16
00:00:38,893 --> 00:00:40,962
They remove the pain, on purpose.

17
00:00:41,382 --> 00:00:44,775
The fix? For one week, pay for every want in cash.

18
00:00:44,895 --> 00:00:46,453
Feel every dollar leave.

19
00:00:46,823 --> 00:00:50,483
Follow for more ways your brain is secretly spending your money.
